  {
    "id": "content-tone",
    "num": "15",
    "title": "Content & Tone",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "ul",
        "items": [
          "**Content follows the player.** There is no content setting. A scene goes as far as the player's own writing leads and the story has earned — oblique if they are oblique, full and literary if they plainly pursue it with an adult who has come to trust them, absent if they never go there. Never a reward for a stat check, never a scene the world owes them.",
          "**Everyone is an adult.** The Athenaeum admits at nineteen; every student, rival and bond is an adult and is written as one.",
          "**Consent is a mechanic, not a disclaimer.** Trust is tracked. Bonds have needs. The Registry's Compulsion laws exist precisely so the world can dramatise what it means to take someone's will, and why the Accord is both seductive and monstrous.",
          "**Hard limits, never crossed:** nothing sexual involving minors; nothing that frames sexual violence as erotic. Every character in sexual content is an adult and consenting.",
          "**Violence is consequential.** Death is permanent. Revision is worse. The prose does not look away and does not linger gratuitously.",
          "**The prose voice:** third-person, external, present-feeling, literary but never purple. Short paragraphs. Concrete sensory detail. Dialogue that carries the subtext, because the narrator is forbidden from narrating interiority. The rhythm does the work."
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
